### Type 2 — The Social Media Creator

**Who they are:**
Someone building an audience on TikTok, Instagram Reels, or YouTube Shorts. Content is their output and volume matters — they need to post consistently, frequently, and at a quality level that keeps people watching. They may have some editing skills but they're not a filmmaker. Speed of production is as important as quality of output.

**What they need from a creative platform:**
High volume, fast turnaround, consistent quality. The ability to take a single piece of raw content and turn it into multiple clips for multiple platforms. Formats that match platform requirements without manual resizing. Tools that produce authentic-feeling content, not obviously AI-generated corporate material.

**Their Bigsfield — the products that matter:**

*Shorts Maker* is the most important Skill in the Supercomputer for this creator. It takes long-form content and automatically cuts it into short clips — finding the hooks, the punchlines, the moments that work in a vertical 60-second format. For a creator who shoots a 20-minute video and needs five clips from it by tonight, this changes everything.

*Video Upscale* ensures their content looks sharp at any size — important when the same clip will be viewed on a phone and a tablet and a desktop.

*Text to Video and Image to Video* serve as content amplifiers — they can generate B-roll, cutaways, and visual context that makes their talking-head or narration content more visually dynamic.

*Viral Presets* stay relevant here too — they use them strategically to ride existing trends rather than just for personal exploration.

*Marketing Studio's Motion and UGC templates* are useful when they're creating sponsored content for a brand partner — ready-to-post formats that meet brand requirements without a design team.

**What they'll never touch:**
Cinema Studio 4.0, Soul Cinema, MCP & CLI, Adobe Plugins (they're not in Premiere), Layers/Edit (too granular for their workflow speed).

**What success looks like:**
Consistent weekly posting. A clip that breaks 100K views. A brand partnership that uses UGC templates to produce the deliverable in under an hour.

**The insight:**
The Social Media Creator represents Bigsfield's largest user segment by volume. They're the ones who make the Community feel alive, generate the most preset-based viral content, and drive peer discovery when followers ask "what tool are you using?" Their use case validates the platform's breadth — they use a genuinely different set of products than the Casual Creator above, and they'll be back tomorrow.

