### Type 6 — The E-commerce / DTC Brand

**Who they are:**
A small to mid-size product brand selling direct-to-consumer — on Shopify, Amazon, Instagram, or all three. They have a physical product and they need content for it constantly: listing images, product videos, social ads, seasonal campaigns. They may not have a full-time creative team. The founder might be doing this themselves.

**What they need from a creative platform:**
Product-focused content that looks like a professional studio shoot without the cost of a professional studio shoot. Formats ready for every channel. Speed, because they're running a business and creative is one of many things on their plate.

**Their Bigsfield — the products that matter:**

*Marketing Studio — Product Shot* is the entry point. Upload a product photo, select a background and context, get a studio-quality image. No photographer, no studio rental, no retoucher.

*Marketing Studio — Motion* animates the product — it floats, rotates, reveals in a way that stops the thumb on a scroll. Static product images perform worse than motion on every major platform. This template bridges that gap without video production.

*Marketing Studio — Marketplace* produces images specifically formatted for Amazon and Shopify product listings — the right dimensions, the right structure, the right visual hierarchy for e-commerce.

*Marketing Studio — UGC* produces authentic creator-style video that performs like influencer content in paid ads — without paying an influencer.

*Ad Multiplier Skill* takes their best performing ad and generates variations for testing — critical for DTC brands running performance campaigns where creative fatigue is a real, measurable problem.

**What they'll never touch:**
Cinema Studio 4.0, Soul Cinema, Faceless Video, MCP & CLI, Canvas, Academy. They want outputs, not craft.

**What success looks like:**
A product launch with a full asset suite produced in a day. An Amazon listing with 8 high-quality product images that would have cost $2,000 to shoot. An ad creative that performs at 3x the previous ROAS because it's finally testing enough variants.

**The insight:**
The E-commerce brand is the use case that Marketing Studio was specifically designed for. The six template categories — Product Shot, Motion, UGC, Ads, Posters, Marketplace — map almost exactly to the creative needs of a DTC product launch. This is a vertical play. Bigsfield isn't positioning as a generic creative tool here — they're positioning as the production studio for e-commerce brands that can't afford a production studio.

