### Type 7 — The Professional Video Editor

**Who they are:**
A freelance video editor or someone at a creative agency. Premiere Pro is their primary tool — they've been using it for years, they have client templates set up, their project organization system is established. They're not looking for a new platform. They are looking for AI generation capability that lives inside their existing workflow.

**What they need from a creative platform:**
Zero workflow disruption. Native integration into their tools. Generation that produces output at the quality level their clients expect — not clearly AI-generated filler.

**Their Bigsfield — the products that matter:**

*Premiere Pro Plugin* is their entire Bigsfield. If this works well — if they can generate a clip, apply an upscale, create a motion graphic, and drop it into their timeline without leaving Premiere — then Bigsfield has won this user. All the platform's generation capabilities become available inside the tool they already use.

*After Effects Plugin* extends this to motion graphics and VFX work — generating elements inside a composition rather than sourcing or creating them from scratch.

*Video Upscale* is particularly useful here — editors regularly receive source footage at insufficient resolution, and Topaz-powered upscaling to 4K is a practical capability they'll use on nearly every project.

*Cinema Studio 4.0* is the generation tool they're most likely to use directly — because they understand cinematic language and the interface speaks that language back to them.

**What they'll never touch:**
Viral Presets, Faceless Video, Marketing Studio, Community, Academy. They came for a specific professional capability, not a platform ecosystem.

**What success looks like:**
A client deliverable that would have taken three extra hours to source or create from scratch — done in twenty minutes with generated assets that met the quality bar.

**The insight:**
The Professional Editor will never become a power user of the Bigsfield website. But they are one of the most valuable user types because of how they discover and spread the product. When a freelancer generates something impressive in Premiere and the client asks "what made that," the next call is the agency asking their tech team to install the plugin for the whole team. One power user becomes twenty. This is peer-driven B2B distribution — and it costs Bigsfield nothing.

