## The Insight This Framework Reveals

The creator-type lens reveals something the journey-stage lens hides: **Bigsfield's biggest risk is not that it does too little. It's that different creator types never discover the products built for them.**

A Filmmaker who lands on the homepage during the Film Festival might sign up and start using Viral Presets — and leave thinking Bigsfield is a preset tool that isn't serious enough for their work. They never saw Cinema Studio 4.0.

An E-commerce founder who signs up for the image generation might use it for basic product shots and never discover Marketing Studio — which would have automated their entire weekly content workflow.

A Developer who hears about Bigsfield as "a video tool" might never investigate the MCP server — which is the only product in their Bigsfield.

**The navigation structure and the homepage communicate one version of Bigsfield.** But there are eight real versions, each one deeply useful to a specific person. Getting the right creator to the right product fast enough is the conversion and retention challenge the product team lives with every day.

